Section I – The poet’s modest aim  
Seek not to dazzle, but to make the world feel seen;  
Let humility guide your pen, and let modesty be your creed.  

Section II – The craft of language  
Choose words as a chef selects herbs—simple, balanced, true;  
Mix them lightly, avoid excess, let each syllable earn its place.  

Section III – The purpose of writing  
Write because the rhythm itself feels right, not for applause or fame;  
When the line lands, the heart answers, and that is enough.  

Section IV – The final polish  
Edit with care, but keep the soul that sparked the thought;  
Trim the excess, preserve the core, and let the piece breathe.

